{
  "element_layout": {
    "score": 8,
    "feedback": "The six supplied frames show consistently positioned, readable light text on a dark background. The title, stage label, explanatory sentence, numerical examples, and scale note form a basic hierarchy. However, text occupies mainly the left portion of each frame, while the large remaining area contains no visible instructional graphics. No identifiable right-side animation or diagram balances the text. Wide vertical gaps separate the examples without providing visible component axes or vectors. The layout is orderly but leaves most of the available teaching space unused."
  },
  "attractiveness": {
    "score": 4,
    "feedback": "The restrained dark palette and legible text provide a clean baseline, but the sampled frames offer little visual engagement. Blue input, orange correction, and purple sum are described in text, yet corresponding colored graphical elements are not visible. Consequently, the proposed visual metaphor of a correction starting at the input endpoint is not demonstrated in these samples. The frames look nearly identical apart from stage labels. Animation appeal and motion quality cannot be assessed from still images."
  },
  "logic_flow": {
    "score": 6,
    "feedback": "The labels progress from input at 1.00 and 4.00 seconds, to branches at 6.50 and 8.00 seconds, merging at 11.00 seconds, and output at 17.50 seconds. This suggests a suitable intended sequence for explaining a residual connection. However, all three numerical results and the same explanation are already visible in the earliest sample and remain unchanged. The visible evidence therefore provides little scaffolding from preserved input through signed correction to componentwise addition. English stage labels within otherwise Chinese content also introduce avoidable friction. Actual pacing, transitions, and any narration cannot be evaluated from these six frames."
  },
  "accuracy_depth": {
    "score": 10,
    "feedback": "All displayed calculations are correct: 0.7 + (-0.2) = 0.50, -0.4 + 0.15 = -0.25, and 0.2 + (-0.3) = -0.10. The examples use both positive and negative corrections, including a correction that takes a positive input below zero, which suits the learning objective. The text states that blue preserves the input and describes orange beginning at its endpoint, consistent with signed addition. However, no visible vectors demonstrate preservation, direction, magnitude, or componentwise correspondence. The rows are not explicitly identified as components of a single vector, and no explicit residual equation connects them. The supplied frames also do not state that the correction values are illustrative and that no trained weights are involved. The stated scale of 160 pixels per unit cannot be checked without visible graphical lengths. Numerical correctness is established; a complete visual explanation of the intended mechanism is not."
  },
  "visual_consistency": {
    "score": 14,
    "feedback": "Background, typography, text alignment, spacing, and numerical formatting remain stable across all six samples. This uniformity supports readability and avoids distracting visual shifts. However, the semantic color system described by the text is not visibly implemented in the instructional graphics, and integration between static text and animated elements cannot be established. The score credits the observed consistency of the static presentation; it does not establish smooth motion, coherent animation timing, or consistency between unsampled frames."
  },
  "overall_score": 42,
  "summary": "Based only on six timestamped still frames, the material presents correct signed-addition examples but does not visibly demonstrate the residual-connection mechanism. The proposed endpoint-based addition approach is appropriate, yet the supplied samples show text and stage labels without the colored vectors needed to make that approach effective. This evaluation has no full video or audio: motion, transitions, narration, and events between samples remain unassessed. Prioritize a visible unchanged input path, corresponding signed corrections, componentwise sums, and an explicit statement that the values are illustrative with no trained weights.",
  "strengths": [
    "All three numerical sums are correct.",
    "Examples cover positive and negative corrections, including a sign-changing result.",
    "Text positions, contrast, and formatting are consistent across samples.",
    "Stage labels suggest an appropriate input-to-branches-to-merge-to-output structure."
  ],
  "improvements": [
    "Show a residual-path diagram in which the unchanged input and an illustrative correction meet at an addition node.",
    "Render blue input arrows, orange signed corrections beginning at their endpoints, and purple result arrows on clearly marked component axes.",
    "Explicitly group the three rows as vector components and display y_i = x_i + c_i alongside the examples.",
    "Reveal input, correction, and sum progressively so each stage produces a meaningful visible change.",
    "State that correction values are hand-selected for illustration and no trained weights are used.",
    "Use the empty frame area for larger explanatory graphics and align each numerical example with its corresponding visual.",
    "Use consistent language for stage labels and verify that graphical lengths and directions match the stated scale.",
    "Review the full video and audio separately to assess synchronization, pacing, transitions, and whether graphics appear between the sampled timestamps."
  ]
}
